# Text is stored with LF whatever the working copy uses, so a clone on another
# machine gets the same bytes. Windows keeps CRLF locally through core.autocrlf.
* text=auto

# The Gradle wrapper is run by sh on Linux and macOS: CRLF in it is a syntax
# error there, and the file is checked out from the repo rather than generated.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Nothing here is text, and letting git guess costs a corrupted PNG eventually.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
*.wgt binary
*.apk binary
